{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' <original-home>/.codex/skills/aristotle-cli/SKILL.md && rg -n -i -C 2 \\\"FF22|finite-range-tracial|I004|Aristotle closeout\\\" <original-home>/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md\"","aggregated_output":"---\nname: aristotle-cli\ndescription: Use when Codex should interact with the Aristotle CLI to submit Lean projects or papers, request sorry filling or formalization runs, inspect job status, and download results for iterative project work.\n---\n\n# Aristotle CLI\n\nUse Aristotle for remote Lean/project runs when the local repo is ready but needs automated proof search, sorry filling, or formalization help.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Confirm the target project or paper from the current workspace.\n2. Check the local build or project state first. Prefer a narrow local `lake build` or equivalent before submitting anything remote.\n3. Use the bundled wrapper `scripts/aristotle-auth.sh` unless `ARISTOTLE_API_KEY` is already known to be exported in the current process.\n4. Submit the smallest useful task prompt. Keep it concrete and tied to the files at hand.\n5. Wait for the result when that is useful. Otherwise poll or list jobs.\n6. Download artifacts, inspect the diffs, and rerun local verification.\n\n## Commands\n\nUse the commands in [references/aristotle-cli.md](references/aristotle-cli.md).\n\n## Operating rules\n\n- Prefer `aristotle submit` for Lean project work, especially sorry filling or proof search.\n- Prefer `aristotle formalize` when the input is a paper or TeX source that should become a Lean artifact.\n- Use `aristotle list` to inspect recent jobs and `aristotle download` to retrieve results.\n- Keep prompts specific: name the file, theorem, section, or proof obligation instead of asking for broad improvement.\n- If a run fails, inspect the local artifact and re-submit only after the prompt or project state is corrected.\n- Do not print or log the API key.\n- If authentication fails but `~/.bashrc` contains the key, do not assume sourcing `.bashrc` works. Many `.bashrc` files return early for noninteractive shells. Use `scripts/aristotle-auth.sh`.\n\n## When to escalate back to the user\n\n- The CLI is missing, or authentication still fails after trying `scripts/aristotle-auth.sh`.\n- The target repo is not a Lean project or paper and needs clarification.\n- The requested action would overwrite user work outside the target project tree.\n945-# Task Group: source-workspace current evidence workflow manual and support-corner theorem statement\n946-\n947:scope: current-only evidence/provenance workflow and the compact I004 Ogata support-corner problem artifact; retain mathematical scope limits and treat the graph as navigation rather than proof\n948:applies_to: cwd=source-workspace; reuse_rule=reuse for live-workflow documentation and this checkout's I004 support-corner investigation, but re-check current TeX/work artifacts before asserting results\n949-\n950-## Task 1: refocus an evidence-acquisition manual on the live project setup\n--\n962-### rollout_summary_files\n963-\n964:- rollout_summaries/2026-07-23T08-24-33-tCl3-general_stabilizer_support_corner_problem_file.md (cwd=source-workspace, rollout_path=<original-home>/.codex/sessions/2026/07/23/rollout-2026-07-23T10-24-33-019f8e13-8cd0-7993-88a1-59c7006bb5c9.jsonl, updated_at=2026-07-23T08:28:59+00:00, thread_id=019f8e13-8cd0-7993-88a1-59c7006bb5c9, one-page compiled I004 problem statement)\n965-\n966-### keywords\n967-\n968:- Ogata, support corner, tracial state, finite exhaustion, strong limit, q M_Gamma q, GNS, type III, I004, PROBLEM.tex, pdflatex\n969-\n970-## User preferences\n--\n980-- For nonfactorial cases, record central measure class, measurable factor field, a.e. fiber type, central support/fullness, and type-III central projection; a trace on one corner alone does not classify the whole algebra. `locator_draft` is pre-normalization; promotion uses stable `source_locator_record` IDs [Task 1]\n981-- For an infinite region `Gamma` exhausted by finite `F_N`, use `M_Gamma = pi_omega(A_Gamma)''`, represented finite support projections `p_N = pi_omega(P_{F_N})`, and strong limit `q`. The general target is a faithful normal trace `tau_q(x)=<Omega,xOmega>` on `q M_Gamma q`, with fullness implying no type-III central summand; it does not automatically prove factoriality or type `II_infinity` [Task 2]\n982:- The compact artifact is `work/2026-07-type-ii-stabilizer-region-algebras/investigations/I004-ogata-surface-code-cone-algebras/PROBLEM.tex`; `pdflatex -interaction=nonstopmode -halt-on-error PROBLEM.tex` plus `pdfinfo` verified a one-page PDF [Task 2]\n983-\n984-## Failures and how to do differently\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' <original-home>/.codex/skills/aristotle-cli/references/aristotle-cli.md && sed -n '1,260p' ../work/2026-08-finite-fiber-von-neumann-formalization/investigations/I004-countable-pauli-quasilocal-realization/aristotle_tasks/FF22-finite-range-tracial-corner-fullness.md && tail -n 150 ../work/2026-08-finite-fiber-von-neumann-formalization/investigations/I004-countable-pauli-quasilocal-realization/HANDOFF.md && tail -n 120 HANDOFF.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' <original-home>/.codex/skills/aristotle-cli/references/aristotle-cli.md && sed -n '1,260p' ../work/2026-08-finite-fiber-von-neumann-formalization/investigations/I004-countable-pauli-quasilocal-realization/aristotle_tasks/FF22-finite-range-tracial-corner-fullness.md && tail -n 150 ../work/2026-08-finite-fiber-von-neumann-formalization/investigations/I004-countable-pauli-quasilocal-realization/HANDOFF.md && tail -n 120 HANDOFF.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Aristotle CLI reference\n\n## Setup\n\n- Install: `uv tool install aristotlelib`\n- Verify: `aristotle --version`\n- Authenticate: set `ARISTOTLE_API_KEY` in the shell environment, or use the skill wrapper `scripts/aristotle-auth.sh`.\n\nIf the key is stored near the end of `~/.bashrc`, noninteractive commands may not see it because many `.bashrc` files contain:\n\n```bash\ncase $- in\n    *i*) ;;\n      *) return;;\nesac\n```\n\nIn that case, do not rely on `source ~/.bashrc`. Use the wrapper, which reads a literal `export ARISTOTLE_API_KEY=...` assignment without printing it:\n\n```bash\n<original-home>/.codex/skills/aristotle-cli/scripts/aristotle-auth.sh formalize input.md\n```\n\n## Core commands\n\nSubmit a Lean project for sorry filling or proof search:\n\n```bash\n<original-home>/.codex/skills/aristotle-cli/scripts/aristotle-auth.sh submit \"Fill in all sorries\" --project-dir ./my-lean-project --wait\n```\n\nFormalize a TeX or paper source:\n\n```bash\n<original-home>/.codex/skills/aristotle-cli/scripts/aristotle-auth.sh formalize paper.tex --wait --destination output.tar.gz\n```\n\nList recent jobs:\n\n```bash\n<original-home>/.codex/skills/aristotle-cli/scripts/aristotle-auth.sh list --limit 10\n```\n\nDownload a completed job:\n\n```bash\n<original-home>/.codex/skills/aristotle-cli/scripts/aristotle-auth.sh download <project-id> --destination result.tar.gz\n```\n\nPass the key directly for one command only:\n\n```bash\naristotle submit \"My prompt\" --api-key \"$ARISTOTLE_API_KEY\" --project-dir ./my-lean-project --wait\n```\n\n## Recommended project loop\n\n1. Inspect the Lean project locally.\n2. Run the narrowest local build or test that exercises the target files.\n3. Submit a focused Aristotle prompt against the project directory.\n4. Wait for the run if the expected result is a concrete patch.\n5. Download or inspect the produced artifact.\n6. Rebuild locally and repeat with a tighter prompt if needed.\n\n## Prompt shape\n\nKeep prompts short and file-bound. Good prompts mention:\n\n- the exact project directory\n- the theorem or file to work on\n- whether to fill `sorry`s, formalize a statement, or debug a failing proof\n- what counts as a useful partial result\n\nAvoid vague prompts such as \"improve this project\" unless the scope is intentionally broad.\n# FF22 — trace and fullness of the finite-range stabilizer corner\n\nRead `manuscript/main.tex` and the outputs of FF20--FF21.  Create only\n`FiniteFiber/FiniteRangeTracialCorner.lean`.\n\nStarting from the concrete finite-range support-corner package of FF21 and the\nfinite full-Pauli/quasilocal/GNS infrastructure, prove the strongest available\nbridge from the canonical stabilizer vector state to a faithful normal positive\ntracial state on `q M q`, and prove that `q` is full.  Work in an explicitly\nsupplied concrete GNS/von-Neumann representation; all normality and strong-limit\nclaims must be stated exactly, not hidden in typeclass inference.\n\nThe mathematical objective is to derive the three substantive FF20 premises:\n\n1. the support-corner vector functional is tracial and faithful on `q M q`;\n2. the support projection is nonzero; and\n3. the orbit/fullness argument gives central support `1`.\n\nFinite range by itself may prove fewer facts than these.  Prove every implication\nyou can, and package any genuinely unavailable bridge as a named explicit\nhypothesis with a counterexample-sensitive explanation.  Do not assert the\nno-type-III conclusion yet; that is FF23.\n\nNo placeholders or new axioms.  Return the complete candidate file, exact\n`lake build` result, and a table of derived versus still conditional premises.\n- `aristotle_responses/FF02-integration-adversarial-review.md`,\n  `aristotle_responses/FF03-integration-adversarial-review.md`, and\n  `aristotle_responses/FF04-integration-adversarial-review.md` approve the\n  three subsequent bounded-operator promotions and the rejection of every\n  remote README insertion.\n- `aristotle_responses/FF05-integration-adversarial-review.md`,\n  `aristotle_responses/FF06-integration-adversarial-review.md`, and\n  `aristotle_responses/FF07-integration-adversarial-review.md` approve the\n  final elementary generator relations and again reject every remote README\n  insertion.\n- `aristotle_responses/FF05-FF07-live-closeout-adversarial-review.md`\n  independently rechecks the live integration, AE/Lp representative handling,\n  theorem scope, permanent status records, and attribution quarantine.\n- `aristotle_responses/FF08-integration-adversarial-review.md` approves the\n  additive initial/tail candidate only and rejects the remote README\n  attribution, stale HANDOFF deletion, and metadata.\n\n## FF13--FF14 closeout\n\nFF13 and FF14 are integrated into `formalization_finite_fibers` after fresh\nadversarial review. The next bounded package is finite-region realization of\n`FullPauliWord` multiplication and its cocycle/central-phase compatibility.\nThe quasilocal algebra, global state, GNS representation, and infinite\nfinite-projection theorem remain unproved.\n\n## Required closeout discipline\n\nBefore saying that any new global bridge is complete:\n\n- add public theorem axioms to `tests/AxiomAudit.lean`;\n- run the narrow target, umbrella build, and full audit;\n- compile the I004 TeX records after material edits;\n- obtain fresh independent mathematical-fidelity and Lean/API adversarial\n  reviews; and\n- keep the distinction between finite directed system, concrete local image,\n  norm closure, state, GNS data, and central-fiber conclusion explicit.\n\n## Worktree notes\n\n- The canonical manuscript at\n  `writing/overleaf_prl_stabilizer_region_algebras/main.tex` was not edited.\n- Existing unrelated dirty and untracked worktree entries were preserved.\n- I004 and `formalization_finite_fibers/` are currently untracked package/work\n  artifacts; no commit or push was made.\n\n## FF15 closeout: finite-region full-Pauli multiplication\n\n**Proved.**  `FiniteFiber/FiniteRegionFullPauliMultiplication.lean` is\nintegrated after quarantine review of Aristotle task\n`f17e2043-2bd3-431a-a76d-8967c9802ef8`.  The main declaration is\n\n```text\nFiniteFiber.fullPauliRegionMatrix_mul\n  (F : Finset Site) (a b : FullPauliWord Site)\n  (ha : a.label.support ⊆ F) :\n  fullPauliRegionMatrix F (a * b) =\n    fullPauliRegionMatrix F a * fullPauliRegionMatrix F b\n```\n\nIt is an exact finite-region matrix multiplication theorem for the existing\nnormal form, with phase correction exactly\n`FullPauliWord.cocycle a.label b.label`.  The left-factor support premise is\nstrong enough for the packet's stated two-word local case.  The module also\nproves `normalFormOneSiteMatrix_mul`, `finiteRegionNormalFormMatrix_mul`,\n`cocycle_eq_finiteRegionNormalFormCocycle`, `fullPauliRegionMatrix_one`, and\n`fullPauliRegionMatrix_negativeIdentity`.\n\n**Partial.**  This does not identify syntactic support with local-algebra\nmembership, prove multi-region representation coherence, construct a directed\ncolimit or norm closure, produce a state or GNS representation, or advance\nthe infinite finite-projection theorem.\n\n**Blocked / failed.**  None within FF15's stated finite-region scope.  The\nremote snapshot's unrelated files and metadata were not integrated.\n\nThe raw archive is quarantined at\n`aristotle_responses/FF15-finite-region-full-pauli-multiplication.tar.gz`;\nthe reviewed candidate module is byte-identical to the live module.  The\nlive verification and adversarial record is\n`aristotle_responses/FF15-live-closeout-adversarial-review.md`.\n\n\n## FF16 closeout: full-Pauli support and finite-region locality\n\n**Proved.** `FiniteFiber/FullPauliSupportLocality.lean` is integrated after quarantine review of Aristotle task `a1684489-8deb-4f62-8f5a-a592570dd778`. For `a : FullPauliWord Site`, it defines `a.SupportedIn F := a.label.support ⊆ F` and a finite-only realization predicate requiring one `A : finiteRegionQubitAlgebra F` to identity-pad to `fullPauliRegionMatrix F' a` for every finite `F ⊆ F'`. It proves\n\n```text\nfiniteRegionEmbed_fullPauliRegionMatrix\n  (F F' : Finset Site) (hFF' : F ⊆ F') (a : FullPauliWord Site)\n  (ha : a.SupportedIn F) :\n  finiteRegionEmbed F F' hFF' (fullPauliRegionMatrix F a) =\n    fullPauliRegionMatrix F' a\n\nsupportedIn_iff_hasFiniteRegionRealization\n  (F : Finset Site) (a : FullPauliWord Site) :\n  a.SupportedIn F ↔ a.HasFiniteRegionRealization F\n```\n\nThe single-region converse has exactly the additional premise `hsupp : a.SupportedIn F'`; it is essential because support outside a chosen `F'` is not visible in its matrix. The final equivalence avoids that failure by taking `F' = F ∪ a.label.support`. The realization is unique and equals `fullPauliRegionMatrix F a`.\n\n**Partial.** This is finite support/local-matrix infrastructure only. It does not identify syntactic support with local-algebra membership, construct a global/quasilocal algebra, state or GNS data, or advance the finite-projection theorem.\n\n**Blocked / failed.** None within FF16 scope. The remote umbrella import, README/metadata, manuscript copy, and every other noncandidate snapshot file were rejected. The raw archive is `aristotle_responses/FF16-full-pauli-support-locality.tar.gz` (SHA-256 `447389053d147319b70c0c519f027c25bfc78c085dcfca68c23e4b793345b727`); the complete snapshot remains at `aristotle_responses/FF16-extracted/`. The integration review is `aristotle_responses/FF16-live-closeout-adversarial-review.md`.\n\nLive checks passed: `lake build FiniteFiber.FullPauliSupportLocality`, `lake build FiniteFiber.FiniteRegionFullPauliMultiplication`, `lake build FiniteFiber`, `lake build`, `lake env lean tests/AxiomAudit.lean`, and a direct `#print axioms` audit for every FF16 public theorem. Each FF16 theorem uses only `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`.\n\n## FF17 closeout: finite stabilizer density from full Pauli words\n\n**Proved.** `FiniteFiber/FullPauliStabilizerDensity.lean` is integrated after\nquarantine review of Aristotle project `a8623a7e-5752-4e4d-9667-d3c741247c1f`,\ntask `44158f6b-4673-4e26-9871-9fc7717c0353`.  For an explicitly finite\n`FullPauliRegionStabilizer`—a subgroup of `FullPauliWord Site`, a finite\nregion, its `Fintype`, supported elements, elementwise involutivity, and\nexclusion of the central word `-1`—the file constructs signed finite-density\ndata and proves the exact basis-reindexed identity\n\n```text\nregionToQubitMatrix D.region D.regionDensity =\n  D.stabilizerData.stabilizerDensity.\n```\n\nHere `regionDensity` is exactly the finite-region group average\n`2^(-|F|) sum_g fullPauliRegionMatrix F g`, with the central `ZMod 4` phase\nand Hermitian normal-form correction converted to the signed-Pauli convention\nof the finite-density layer.  Positivity, trace one, the normalized-projector\nformula, projector invariance, and nonzeroness follow.  The optional global\nconstructor keeps its premises visible: every global group member must square\nto one and `-1` must be excluded.  The generator constructor discharges those\nonly from the existing pairwise-commuting, order-two, consistent generator\ndata.\n\n**Partial.** This establishes only the manuscript's single finite-region\ndensity identity.  It proves neither multi-region partial-trace compatibility\nnor a quasilocal completion, global state, GNS construction, normality, or the\nfinite-fiber conclusion.\n\n**Blocked / failed.** None within FF17's stated scope.  The raw archive is\n`aristotle_responses/FF17-full-pauli-stabilizer-density.tar.gz` (SHA-256\n`7e86f988e2118b9e43141f319f65b9ccf5ae0802be34147d670212acdfc84a63`), and\nthe complete dependency-free snapshot remains quarantined at\n`aristotle_responses/FF17-extracted/`.  Only the candidate Lean module was\nintegrated; remote README attribution, metadata, and manuscript copy were\nrejected.  The complete adversarial review is\n`aristotle_responses/FF17-live-closeout-adversarial-review.md`.\n\nLive checks passed: `lake build FiniteFiber.FullPauliStabilizerDensity`, its\nthree direct predecessor targets, `lake build FiniteFiber`, `lake build`, and\n`lake env lean tests/AxiomAudit.lean`.  A direct audit covered every one of\nthe 41 public FF17 theorems; each uses only `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and\n`Quot.sound`, and the target module has no placeholder/prohibited declaration.\n\n## Current verification record\n\nThe checked finite-group/support-corner core is complete as of August 3, 2026.  Reproduce its\nverification from this package directory with:\n\n```bash\nlake build FiniteFiber.Basic\nlake build FiniteFiber.TracialCorner\nlake build FiniteFiber.FiniteFibers\nlake build FiniteFiber.FiniteStabilizer\nlake build FiniteFiber.FiniteStabilizerTrace\nlake build FiniteFiber.FinitePauli\nlake build FiniteFiber.FiniteQubitMatrix\nlake build FiniteFiber.FiniteDensity\nlake build FiniteFiber.FinitePauliStabilizer\nlake build FiniteFiber.FinitePauliGNS\nlake build FiniteFiber.FiniteLocalPauli\nlake build FiniteFiber.FiniteNestedPauli\nlake build FiniteFiber.FiniteLocalGroupSupport\nlake build FiniteFiber.ProjectivePauliLattice\nlake build FiniteFiber.FullPauliLattice\nlake build FiniteFiber.OneSitePauliNormalForm\nlake build FiniteFiber.FiniteTensorMatrixChain\nlake build FiniteFiber.FiniteRegionQubitAlgebra\nlake build FiniteFiber.FiniteRegionPauliMatrices\nlake build FiniteFiber.FiniteNestedTensorState\nlake build FiniteFiber.FiniteStabilizerStateChain\nlake build FiniteFiber.SequentialLocalFunctional\nlake build FiniteFiber.CountablePauliRepresentation\nlake build FiniteFiber.StrongSupport\nlake build FiniteFiber.StabilizerSequence\nlake build FiniteFiber.VectorCorner\nlake build FiniteFiber.GNSVector\nlake build FiniteFiber.GNSOrbit\nlake build FiniteFiber.StabilizerFiniteFiber\nlake build\nlake env lean tests/AxiomAudit.lean\n```\n\nThe audit is expected to report only `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and\n`Quot.sound`.  The independent closeout reports are at:\n\n- `../work/2026-08-finite-fiber-von-neumann-formalization/investigations/I001-full-tracial-corner/reviews/math_fidelity_review.md`\n- `../work/2026-08-finite-fiber-von-neumann-formalization/investigations/I001-full-tracial-corner/reviews/lean_api_review.md`\n\nThe approved I002 adversarial reports are:\n\n- `../work/2026-08-finite-fiber-von-neumann-formalization/investigations/I002-stabilizer-gns-realization/reviews/math_fidelity_review.md`\n- `../work/2026-08-finite-fiber-von-neumann-formalization/investigations/I002-stabilizer-gns-realization/reviews/lean_api_review.md`\n\nThe I003 finite-Pauli/density investigation and its adversarial reports are:\n\n- `../work/2026-08-finite-fiber-von-neumann-formalization/investigations/I003-finite-pauli-density-realization/technical.tex`\n- `../work/2026-08-finite-fiber-von-neumann-formalization/investigations/I003-finite-pauli-density-realization/reviews/math_fidelity_review.md`\n- `../work/2026-08-finite-fiber-von-neumann-formalization/investigations/I003-finite-pauli-density-realization/reviews/lean_api_review.md`\n- `../work/2026-08-finite-fiber-von-neumann-formalization/investigations/I003-finite-pauli-density-realization/reviews/finite_sequential_directed_system_math_fidelity_review.md`\n- `../work/2026-08-finite-fiber-von-neumann-formalization/investigations/I003-finite-pauli-density-realization/reviews/finite_sequential_directed_system_lean_api_review.md`\n- `../work/2026-08-finite-fiber-von-neumann-formalization/investigations/I003-finite-pauli-density-realization/reviews/finite_sequential_norm_math_fidelity_review.md`\n- `../work/2026-08-finite-fiber-von-neumann-formalization/investigations/I003-finite-pauli-density-realization/reviews/finite_sequential_norm_lean_api_review.md`\n\n## FF13--FF14 integration\n\nFF13 and FF14 are integrated and independently adversarially approved.\n`FiniteRegionPhasedPauliMatrices.lean` proves the finite-region summed-phase\nnormal form and identity padding. `FiniteRegionEmbeddingCoherence.lean`\nproves the explicit entrywise restriction formula and directed-system\ncoherence for `finiteRegionEmbed`. Both remain finite-region statements;\nfull-word multiplication, support/locality, quasilocal completion, state, and\nGNS construction remain open.\n\nVerification passed:\n\n```bash\nlake env lean FiniteFiber/FiniteRegionEmbeddingCoherence.lean\nlake env lean FiniteFiber/FiniteRegionPhasedPauliMatrices.lean\nlake build FiniteFiber.FiniteRegionEmbeddingCoherence\nlake build FiniteFiber.FiniteRegionPhasedPauliMatrices\nlake build FiniteFiber\nlake env lean tests/AxiomAudit.lean\nlake build\n```\n\nAristotle archive metadata claiming commit/push was not integrated.\n\n## FF15 finite-region full-Pauli multiplication closeout\n\nFF15 is accepted and integrated as\n`FiniteFiber/FiniteRegionFullPauliMultiplication.lean`.  The quarantined\narchive SHA-256 is\n`d1189115efff732746653b26166b1c89a8e9c38b3d5af266c27b158db2ddc02f`;\nthe candidate module SHA-256 is\n`bfa680e974985ce9e040cb0e7c93eb7bf828fa892be1e76131abc9a548cc7d94` and is\nbyte-identical to the live module.  Only that module and the raw archive were\nadopted; remote metadata and all unrelated snapshot files remain quarantined.\n\nThe checked theorem `fullPauliRegionMatrix_mul F a b ha` has the explicit\npremise `ha : a.label.support ⊆ F` and proves\n`fullPauliRegionMatrix F (a * b) = fullPauliRegionMatrix F a *\nfullPauliRegionMatrix F b`.  Its phase is the existing\n`FullPauliWord.cocycle a.label b.label`; it therefore covers the packet's\nintended case in which both words are supported in `F`.  The module also\nproves the one-site raw `X`-then-`Z` multiplication relation, finite-region\nprojective multiplication, the identity-word image, and the image of\n`FullPauliWord.negativeIdentity`.  It does not construct a support/local-\nalgebra identification, directed colimit, quasilocal completion, state/GNS\ndata, or finite-fiber conclusion.\n\nVerification passed:\n\n```bash\nlake build FiniteFiber.FiniteRegionFullPauliMultiplication\nlake build\nlake env lean tests/AxiomAudit.lean\nlake env lean tests/FullPauliMultiplicationAxiomAudit.lean\n```\n\nBoth audits report only `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`.  The\ncloseout review is at\n`../work/2026-08-finite-fiber-von-neumann-formalization/investigations/I004-countable-pauli-quasilocal-realization/aristotle_responses/FF15-live-closeout-adversarial-review.md`.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
