{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'remote=../work/2026-08-finite-fiber-von-neumann-formalization/investigations/I004-countable-pauli-quasilocal-realization/aristotle_responses/FF22-extracted/aristotle-finite_fiber-jwxyqzjl_aristotle; sha256sum \"$remote/FiniteFiber/FiniteRangeTracialCorner.lean\"; sed -n '\"'1,280p' \\\"\"'$remote/FiniteFiber/FiniteRangeTracialCorner.lean\"; sed -n '\"'1,260p' FiniteFiber/FiniteRangeSupportCornerConstruction.lean; sed -n '1,220p' \\\"\"'$remote/ARISTOTLE_SUMMARY.md\"; diff -u FiniteFiber.lean \"$remote/FiniteFiber.lean\" || true; diff -u HANDOFF.md \"$remote/HANDOFF.md\" | sed -n '\"'1,180p' || true\"","aggregated_output":"ff7797b79959e186083b9d408a5e5a5547b1195a9517edf97657f033d574b562  ../work/2026-08-finite-fiber-von-neumann-formalization/investigations/I004-countable-pauli-quasilocal-realization/aristotle_responses/FF22-extracted/aristotle-finite_fiber-jwxyqzjl_aristotle/FiniteFiber/FiniteRangeTracialCorner.lean\nimport FiniteFiber.FiniteRangeSupportCornerConstruction\n\n/-!\n# Trace and fullness of the finite-range stabilizer corner\n\nThis file (FF22) takes the concrete finite-range support-corner package of FF21\n(`FiniteFiber.FiniteRangeStabilizerSystem`, its decreasing local code-space\nsupports `p n = π_ω(P_{Γ_n})` and their canonical strong limit `q`) and proves,\ninside an *explicitly supplied* concrete GNS/von-Neumann representation, the\nthree substantive premises which FF20 (`FiniteFiber.GNSOrbitConditions`) still\nhad to assume:\n\n1. the support-corner vector functional `τ_q(x) = ⟪Ω, x Ω⟫` is **tracial** and\n   **faithful** on `q M q`;\n2. the support projection `q` is **nonzero**;\n3. the orbit argument makes `q` **full** (central support `1`).\n\nEverything is stated for the concrete operator model: `M` is a\n`VonNeumannAlgebra` on the GNS space `W.GNS`, all limits are the explicit\npointwise strong limits of `FiniteFiber.StrongSupport`, and normality is stated\nas an exact strong-convergence continuity statement rather than being hidden in\na typeclass.\n\n## Infrastructure developed here\n\n* `FiniteFiber.exists_mem_norm_sub_apply_lt`: a **von Neumann density theorem**\n  (the finite-tuple strong approximation form of the bicommutant theorem),\n  proved from scratch by the amplification argument.  Mathlib only has the\n  tautological `VonNeumannAlgebra.commutant_commutant`.\n* the exact normality, positivity and normalization statements for the corner\n  vector functional;\n* the passage from corner traciality to *full* faithfulness on `q M q`\n  (Proposition `prop:faithful` of the manuscript, for arbitrary corner\n  elements, not only projections);\n* the finite-volume trace-cyclicity identity for the local code projector and\n  its strong-limit consequence, i.e. Lemma `lem:finite-trace` of the\n  manuscript.\n\n## Hypotheses\n\nFor a *general* von Neumann algebra `M` satisfying the FF21 hypothesis `hM`\n(`M` contains the represented finite local algebras), traciality on all of\n`q M q` uses exactly one further hypothesis, namely that `M` really is the\nmanuscript's `M_Γ = 𝒰_Γ''`: every element of `M` commutes with every operator\ncommuting with the represented local algebra\n(`QuasilocalStabilizerState.GeneratedByLocalAlgebra`).  This is a *definitional*\nidentification of `M`, not an analytic gap, and it cannot simply be deleted: for\na strictly larger `M` (for instance all of `B(H)`, which still satisfies `hM`)\nthe argument below produces the local symmetry only inside the strong closure of\nthe local algebra, so the vector state on the corner need not be tracial.\n\nFor the **canonical** choice `M = M_Γ`, which is the algebra the manuscript\nworks with, the hypothesis is *discharged*: `Part I'` constructs the bicommutant\nof a star subalgebra of `B(H)` as a von Neumann algebra, and\n`QuasilocalStabilizerState.localVonNeumannAlgebra` is exactly\n`π_ω(𝒜_loc)''`.  Consequently\n`FiniteRangeStabilizerSystem.supportCornerConclusion_localVonNeumannAlgebra`\ncarries *no* hypothesis beyond the FF21 data `R`, `Q`, `W`.\n\nNo no-type-III statement is made here; that is FF23.\n-/\n\nnamespace FiniteFiber\n\nopen scoped InnerProductSpace\nopen Filter Topology\n\n/-! ## Part I. A von Neumann density theorem\n\nMathlib does not contain the von Neumann bicommutant/density theorem, only the\ndefinitional `VonNeumannAlgebra.commutant_commutant`.  The finite-tuple strong\napproximation statement below is proved here by the standard amplification\nargument; it is the only nontrivial operator-topological input to the\ntraciality proof and it replaces the Kaplansky-density step of the manuscript.\n-/\n\nsection Density\n\nvariable {H : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup H] [InnerProductSpace ℂ H] [CompleteSpace H]\n\n/-- The `n`-fold diagonal amplification of a bounded operator. -/\nnoncomputable def amplify (n : ℕ) (a : H →L[ℂ] H) :\n    (PiLp 2 fun _ : Fin n => H) →L[ℂ] (PiLp 2 fun _ : Fin n => H) :=\n  (PiLp.continuousLinearEquiv 2 ℂ (fun _ : Fin n => H)).symm.toContinuousLinearMap ∘L\n    (ContinuousLinearMap.pi fun i => a ∘L PiLp.proj 2 (fun _ : Fin n => H) i)\n\nomit [CompleteSpace H] in\n@[simp] lemma amplify_apply (n : ℕ) (a : H →L[ℂ] H)\n    (v : PiLp 2 fun _ : Fin n => H) (i : Fin n) : (amplify n a v) i = a (v i) := rfl\n\n/-- The `j`-th coordinate inclusion into the amplified Hilbert space. -/\nnoncomputable def amplifyInj (n : ℕ) (j : Fin n) : H →L[ℂ] (PiLp 2 fun _ : Fin n => H) :=\n  (PiLp.continuousLinearEquiv 2 ℂ (fun _ : Fin n => H)).symm.toContinuousLinearMap ∘L\n    ContinuousLinearMap.single ℂ (fun _ : Fin n => H) j\n\nomit [CompleteSpace H] in\nlemma amplifyInj_apply (n : ℕ) (j : Fin n) (v : H) (i : Fin n) :\n    (amplifyInj n j v) i = if i = j then v else 0 := by\n  classical\n  simp [amplifyInj, ContinuousLinearMap.single, Pi.single_apply]\n\nomit [CompleteSpace H] in\nlemma sum_amplifyInj (n : ℕ) (v : PiLp 2 fun _ : Fin n => H) :\n    ∑ j, amplifyInj n j (v j) = v := by\n  classical\n  ext i\n  simp [amplifyInj, ContinuousLinearMap.single, Pi.single_apply]\n\nomit [CompleteSpace H] in\nlemma amplify_one (n : ℕ) : amplify n (1 : H →L[ℂ] H) = 1 := by\n  ext v i; rfl\n\nomit [CompleteSpace H] in\nlemma amplify_zero (n : ℕ) : amplify n (0 : H →L[ℂ] H) = 0 := by\n  ext v i; rfl\n\nomit [CompleteSpace H] in\nlemma amplify_add (n : ℕ) (a b : H →L[ℂ] H) :\n    amplify n (a + b) = amplify n a + amplify n b := by\n  ext v i; rfl\n\nomit [CompleteSpace H] in\nlemma amplify_smul (n : ℕ) (c : ℂ) (a : H →L[ℂ] H) :\n    amplify n (c • a) = c • amplify n a := by\n  ext v i; rfl\n\nomit [CompleteSpace H] in\nlemma amplify_mul (n : ℕ) (a b : H →L[ℂ] H) :\n    amplify n (a * b) = amplify n a * amplify n b := by\n  ext v i; rfl\n\nlemma amplify_star (n : ℕ) (a : H →L[ℂ] H) :\n    amplify n (star a) = star (amplify n a) := by\n  have hinner : ∀ (u v : PiLp 2 fun _ : Fin n => H),\n      ⟪amplify n (star a) u, v⟫_ℂ = ⟪u, amplify n a v⟫_ℂ := by\n    intro u v\n    rw [PiLp.inner_apply, PiLp.inner_apply]\n    refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ => ?_\n    show ⟪star a (u i), v i⟫_ℂ = ⟪u i, a (v i)⟫_ℂ\n    rw [ContinuousLinearMap.star_eq_adjoint, ContinuousLinearMap.adjoint_inner_left]\n  apply ContinuousLinearMap.ext\n  intro u\n  apply ext_inner_right (𝕜 := ℂ)\n  intro v\n  rw [hinner u v, ContinuousLinearMap.star_eq_adjoint, ContinuousLinearMap.adjoint_inner_left]\n\nomit [CompleteSpace H] in\nlemma amplify_amplifyInj (n : ℕ) (a : H →L[ℂ] H) (j : Fin n) (v : H) :\n    amplify n a (amplifyInj n j v) = amplifyInj n j (a v) := by\n  classical\n  ext i\n  rw [amplify_apply, amplifyInj_apply, amplifyInj_apply]\n  by_cases h : i = j <;> simp [h]\n\n/-- The `(i,j)` operator entry of an operator on the amplified Hilbert space. -/\nnoncomputable def amplifyEntry (n : ℕ)\n    (T : (PiLp 2 fun _ : Fin n => H) →L[ℂ] (PiLp 2 fun _ : Fin n => H)) (i j : Fin n) :\n    H →L[ℂ] H :=\n  PiLp.proj 2 (fun _ : Fin n => H) i ∘L T ∘L amplifyInj n j\n\nomit [CompleteSpace H] in\nlemma amplifyEntry_apply (n : ℕ)\n    (T : (PiLp 2 fun _ : Fin n => H) →L[ℂ] (PiLp 2 fun _ : Fin n => H)) (i j : Fin n)\n    (v : H) : amplifyEntry n T i j v = (T (amplifyInj n j v)) i := rfl\n\nomit [CompleteSpace H] in\nlemma apply_coord_eq_sum_amplifyEntry (n : ℕ)\n    (T : (PiLp 2 fun _ : Fin n => H) →L[ℂ] (PiLp 2 fun _ : Fin n => H))\n    (v : PiLp 2 fun _ : Fin n => H) (i : Fin n) :\n    (T v) i = ∑ j, amplifyEntry n T i j (v j) := by\n  conv_lhs => rw [← sum_amplifyInj n v]\n  rw [map_sum]\n  simp [amplifyEntry_apply]\n\nomit [CompleteSpace H] in\n/-- If `T` commutes with the amplification of every element of a set of operators, then all\nits operator entries commute with that set. -/\nlemma amplifyEntry_commutes (n : ℕ) (𝒜 : Set (H →L[ℂ] H))\n    {T : (PiLp 2 fun _ : Fin n => H) →L[ℂ] (PiLp 2 fun _ : Fin n => H)}\n    (hT : ∀ a ∈ 𝒜, amplify n a * T = T * amplify n a) (i j : Fin n) :\n    ∀ a ∈ 𝒜, a * amplifyEntry n T i j = amplifyEntry n T i j * a := by\n  intro a ha\n  apply ContinuousLinearMap.ext\n  intro v\n  have h := congrArg (fun S => S (amplifyInj n j v)) (hT a ha)\n  simp only at h\n  have h' : (amplify n a (T (amplifyInj n j v))) i = (T (amplify n a (amplifyInj n j v))) i :=\n    congrArg (fun w : PiLp 2 fun _ : Fin n => H => w i) h\n  rw [amplify_apply, amplify_amplifyInj] at h'\n  exact h'\n\nomit [CompleteSpace H] in\n/-- If every operator entry of `T` commutes with `x`, then `T` commutes with the amplification\nof `x`. -/\nlemma amplify_commutes_of_amplifyEntry (n : ℕ) {x : H →L[ℂ] H}\n    {T : (PiLp 2 fun _ : Fin n => H) →L[ℂ] (PiLp 2 fun _ : Fin n => H)}\n    (h : ∀ i j, x * amplifyEntry n T i j = amplifyEntry n T i j * x) :\n    amplify n x * T = T * amplify n x := by\n  apply ContinuousLinearMap.ext\n  intro v\n  ext i\n  show x ((T v) i) = (T (amplify n x v)) i\n  rw [apply_coord_eq_sum_amplifyEntry, apply_coord_eq_sum_amplifyEntry, map_sum]\n  refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun j _ => ?_\n  exact congrArg (fun S : H →L[ℂ] H => S (v j)) (h i j)\n\n/--\n**The von Neumann density theorem, finite-tuple strong form.**  If `x` commutes with every\noperator commuting with a unital `*`-subalgebra `𝒜` of `B(H)` — that is, if `x ∈ 𝒜''` — then\n`x` is approximated by an element of `𝒜` on any finite tuple of vectors.\n\nThis is the operator-topological input which the manuscript obtains from Kaplansky's density\ntheorem; Mathlib contains neither statement, so it is proved here by amplification.\n-/\ntheorem exists_mem_norm_sub_apply_lt\n    (𝒜 : StarSubalgebra ℂ (H →L[ℂ] H)) {x : H →L[ℂ] H}\n    (hx : ∀ t : H →L[ℂ] H, (∀ a ∈ 𝒜, a * t = t * a) → x * t = t * x)\n    {n : ℕ} (ξ : Fin n → H) {ε : ℝ} (hε : 0 < ε) :\n    ∃ u ∈ 𝒜, ∀ i, ‖x (ξ i) - u (ξ i)‖ < ε := by\n  classical\n  set Xi : PiLp 2 (fun _ : Fin n => H) := WithLp.toLp 2 ξ with hXi\n  have hXi_apply : ∀ i, Xi i = ξ i := fun i => rfl\n  let V : Submodule ℂ (PiLp 2 fun _ : Fin n => H) :=\n    { carrier := {v | ∃ a ∈ 𝒜, amplify n a Xi = v}\n      add_mem' := by\n        rintro u v ⟨a, ha, rfl⟩ ⟨b, hb, rfl⟩\n        exact ⟨a + b, add_mem ha hb, by rw [amplify_add]; rfl⟩\n      zero_mem' := ⟨0, zero_mem _, by rw [amplify_zero]; rfl⟩\n      smul_mem' := by\n        rintro c v ⟨a, ha, rfl⟩\n        exact ⟨c • a, SMulMemClass.smul_mem c ha, by rw [amplify_smul]; rfl⟩ }\n  set K := V.topologicalClosure with hK\n  set P := K.starProjection with hP\n  have hinvV : ∀ a ∈ 𝒜, ∀ v ∈ V, amplify n a v ∈ V := by\n    rintro a ha v ⟨b, hb, rfl⟩\n    exact ⟨a * b, mul_mem ha hb, by rw [amplify_mul]; rfl⟩\n  have hinvK : ∀ a ∈ 𝒜, ∀ v ∈ K, amplify n a v ∈ K := by\n    intro a ha v hv\n    have hmap : (V : Set (PiLp 2 fun _ : Fin n => H)) ⊆ (amplify n a) ⁻¹' (K : Set _) :=\n      fun w hw => Submodule.le_topologicalClosure V (hinvV a ha w hw)\n    have hclosed : IsClosed ((amplify n a) ⁻¹' (K : Set _)) :=\n      (V.isClosed_topologicalClosure).preimage (amplify n a).continuous\n    have hsub : (K : Set (PiLp 2 fun _ : Fin n => H)) ⊆ (amplify n a) ⁻¹' (K : Set _) := by\n      rw [hK, Submodule.topologicalClosure_coe]\n      exact closure_minimal hmap hclosed\n    exact hsub hv\n  have hPcomm : ∀ a ∈ 𝒜, amplify n a * P = P * amplify n a := by\n    have key : ∀ a ∈ 𝒜, P * amplify n a * P = amplify n a * P := by\n      intro a ha\n      apply ContinuousLinearMap.ext\n      intro v\n      show P (amplify n a (P v)) = amplify n a (P v)\n      exact Submodule.starProjection_eq_self_iff.mpr\n        (hinvK a ha _ (K.starProjection_apply_mem v))\n    intro a ha\n    have h1 := key a ha\n    have h2 := key (star a) (star_mem ha)\n    have hPsa : star P = P := (isSelfAdjoint_starProjection K).star_eq\n    have h2' : P * star (amplify n a) * P = star (amplify n a) * P := by\n      rw [← amplify_star]; exact h2\n    have h3 : P * amplify n a * P = P * amplify n a := by\n      have h4 := congrArg star h2'\n      simpa [star_mul, hPsa, star_star, mul_assoc] using h4\n    rw [← h1, h3]\n  have hentry : ∀ i j, x * amplifyEntry n P i j = amplifyEntry n P i j * x := fun i j =>\n    hx _ (amplifyEntry_commutes n (𝒜 : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)) hPcomm i j)\n  have hxP : amplify n x * P = P * amplify n x := amplify_commutes_of_amplifyEntry n hentry\n  have hXiK : Xi ∈ K := by\n    refine Submodule.le_topologicalClosure V ⟨1, one_mem _, ?_⟩\n    rw [amplify_one]; rfl\n  have hPXi : P Xi = Xi := Submodule.starProjection_eq_self_iff.mpr hXiK\n  have hxXi : amplify n x Xi ∈ K := by\n    have hrw : amplify n x Xi = P (amplify n x Xi) := by\n      conv_lhs => rw [← hPXi]\n      exact congrArg (fun S : (PiLp 2 fun _ : Fin n => H) →L[ℂ] (PiLp 2 fun _ : Fin n => H) =>\n        S Xi) hxP\n    rw [hrw]\n    exact K.starProjection_apply_mem _\n  have hmem : amplify n x Xi ∈ closure (V : Set (PiLp 2 fun _ : Fin n => H)) := by\n    rw [← Submodule.topologicalClosure_coe]\nimport FiniteFiber.ActualStabilizerSupportCorner\n\n/-!\n# The finite-range geometric input for the support-corner construction\n\nThis file supplies the *geometric* data that\n`FiniteFiber.ActualStabilizerSupportCorner` (FF20) still had to assume by hand:\na countable, locally finite lattice together with a **finite-range** consistent\nstabilizer system, an explicit exhaustion of the lattice by finite regions, the\nresulting increasing sequence of **finite** local stabilizer subgroups, and the\ndecreasing sequence of local code-space support projections in the supplied GNS\noperator model, with its canonical strong limit.\n\n## The data\n\n`FiniteRangeStabilizerSystem Site` bundles\n\n* a surjective enumeration `enumerate : ℕ → Site` (countability of the lattice);\n* a finite `neighborhood : Site → Finset Site` with `s ∈ neighborhood s`\n  (local finiteness: the range-`r` ball around a site is a finite region);\n* pairwise-commuting involutive full-Pauli generators whose generated group\n  omits `-1` (`FullPauliWord.StabilizerGeneratorData`, i.e. the manuscript's\n  consistent stabilizer system); and\n* the **finite-range condition** `generator_range`: every generator is\n  supported inside a single neighborhood ball.\n\n## What is proved here from that data alone\n\n* `FiniteRangeStabilizerSystem.region` is a monotone exhaustion of `Site` by\n  finite regions, each of which is a finite union of range balls\n  (`region_mono`, `mem_region`, `exhaustion`).\n* Finite range gives the *one-ball* statement\n  `generator_supportedIn_region`: each generator already sits in the stage\n  `k + 1` determined by the single site index enumerating the centre of its\n  ball.  (For an arbitrary finite-support stabilizer one only gets the weaker\n  `exists_region_superset`, which needs an induction over the finite support.)\n* `localStabilizer n`, the group of global stabilizers supported in\n  `region n`, is a subgroup of the global stabilizer group; it is **finite**\n  (`localStabilizerFintype`), the sequence is increasing\n  (`localStabilizer_mono`), and it exhausts the global stabilizer group\n  (`exists_mem_localStabilizer`, `iSup_localStabilizer`).\n* In the supplied GNS model of a `QuasilocalStabilizerState`, the local\n  code-space supports `supportProjection W n = π_ω(P_{Γ_n})` form a decreasing\n  sequence of projections in any von Neumann algebra `M` containing the\n  represented finite local algebras, each fixes `Ω`, and each is nonzero\n  (`supportProjectionSequence`, `supportProjection_gnsVector`,\n  `supportProjection_ne_zero`).\n* Their strong limit exists and is *constructed*, not assumed: the canonical\n  `decreasingProjectionStrongLimit` of `FiniteFiber.StrongSupport` is a\n  projection in `M`, fixes `Ω`, and is therefore **nonzero**\n  (`cornerProjection_isProjectionIn`, `cornerProjection_gnsVector`,\n  `cornerProjection_ne_zero`).  No strong-limit premise is needed.\n\n* **Non-vacuity**: `natAllZFiniteRangeSystem` is an explicit finite-range\n  consistent stabilizer system on the countably infinite lattice `ℕ` (the\n  all-`Z` code, range zero) with nontrivial finite local stabilizer groups.\n\nAll of that is collected in `FiniteRangeSupportCornerData` and produced by\n`FiniteRangeStabilizerSystem.supportCornerData`; feeding it to FF20 gives\n`finiteRange_supportCornerConclusion_of_gnsOrbit`.\n\n## What finite range does *not* give\n\nThe remaining inputs are exactly the analytic/global ones, and they stay\nexplicit premises:\n\n* the quasilocal C-star completion `Q` and the global state `W` (existence of\n  the state is Proposition `prop:define_state` of the manuscript; it is an\n  interface input here);\n* the von Neumann algebra `M` with `hM`;\n* `GNSOrbitConditions M q Ω`: the regional/complementary commutation data, the\n  dense product orbit (fullness of `q`) and traciality of the compressed vector\n  functional on corner elements.\n\nAlso isolated here is the *local-code consistency* condition\n`FiniteRangeStabilizerSystem.LocallyGenerated`: that the stabilizers supported\nin `region n` are exactly the products of generators supported in `region n`.\nOnly the easy inclusion\n`closure_localGenerators_le_regionStabilizer` follows from finite range; the\nconverse is an extra hypothesis, and it is what identifies the abstract local\ncode projection `P_{Γ_n}` with the projection built from the generators of the\ncode inside `Γ_n`.  None of the results below need it, because nonzeroness of\neach `p n` is obtained from the fixed GNS vector instead; it is recorded because\nany *local* computation of the code space (dimension counting, local\nindependence of generators) does need it.\n\nNo trace, fullness, type classification or no-type-III statement is claimed in\nthis file.\n-/\n\nnamespace FiniteFiber\n\nopen scoped InnerProductSpace\n\nvariable {Site : Type*} [DecidableEq Site]\n\n/-! ### The finite-range lattice/stabilizer data -/\n\n/--\n**A countable locally finite lattice with a finite-range consistent stabilizer\nsystem.**  The lattice is presented by a surjective enumeration and by finite\nneighbourhood balls containing their centres; the stabilizer system is a\n`FullPauliWord.StabilizerGeneratorData` (pairwise commuting involutive\ngenerators generating a group without `-1`) whose generators each fit inside a\nsingle ball.\n-/\nstructure FiniteRangeStabilizerSystem (Site : Type*) [DecidableEq Site] extends\n    FullPauliWord.StabilizerGeneratorData Site where\n  /-- A surjective enumeration of the lattice sites: the lattice is countable. -/\n  enumerate : ℕ → Site\n  /-- Every site is enumerated. -/\n  enumerate_surjective : Function.Surjective enumerate\n  /-- The finite range ball around a site: local finiteness of the lattice. -/\n  neighborhood : Site → Finset Site\n  /-- A site belongs to its own ball. -/\n  self_mem_neighborhood : ∀ s, s ∈ neighborhood s\n  /-- **Finite range**: every generator is supported inside a single ball. -/\n  generator_range : ∀ g ∈ generators, ∃ s : Site, g.label.support ⊆ neighborhood s\n\nnamespace FiniteRangeStabilizerSystem\n\nvariable (R : FiniteRangeStabilizerSystem Site)\n\n/-! #### The exhaustion by finite regions -/\n\n/-- The `n`-th finite region: the union of the balls around the first `n`\nenumerated sites. -/\ndef region (n : ℕ) : Finset Site :=\n  (Finset.range n).biUnion fun k => R.neighborhood (R.enumerate k)\n\ntheorem mem_region_iff (n : ℕ) (s : Site) :\n    s ∈ R.region n ↔ ∃ k < n, s ∈ R.neighborhood (R.enumerate k) := by\n  simp [region, Finset.mem_biUnion, Finset.mem_range]\n\n/-- The regions increase. -/\ntheorem region_mono : Monotone R.region := by\n  intro n m hnm s hs\n  rw [mem_region_iff] at hs ⊢\n  obtain ⟨k, hk, hsk⟩ := hs\n  exact ⟨k, lt_of_lt_of_le hk hnm, hsk⟩\n\n/-- The ball around the `k`-th enumerated site is already a subregion of stage\n`k + 1`. -/\ntheorem neighborhood_subset_region (k : ℕ) :\n    R.neighborhood (R.enumerate k) ⊆ R.region (k + 1) := by\n  intro s hs\n  exact (R.mem_region_iff _ s).mpr ⟨k, Nat.lt_succ_self k, hs⟩\n\n/-- Every site is covered by some finite stage. -/\ntheorem mem_region (s : Site) : ∃ n, s ∈ R.region n := by\n  obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := R.enumerate_surjective s\n  exact ⟨k + 1, R.neighborhood_subset_region k (hk ▸ R.self_mem_neighborhood s)⟩\n\n/-- The regions form a finite-region exhaustion of the lattice. -/\ndef exhaustion : ProjectivePauliWord.FiniteExhaustion Site where\n  region := R.region\n  mono := R.region_mono\n  cover := R.mem_region\n\n/-- Every finite set of sites is contained in a stage of the exhaustion. -/\ntheorem exists_region_superset (F : Finset Site) : ∃ n, F ⊆ R.region n :=\n  R.exhaustion.covers_finset F\n\n/--\n**The finite-range statement.**  A generator supported in the ball around\n`enumerate k` is supported in the single region `region (k + 1)`; no induction\nover its support is needed.\n-/\ntheorem generator_supportedIn_region {g : FullPauliWord Site} (hg : g ∈ R.generators) :\n    ∃ n, g.label.support ⊆ R.region n := by\n  obtain ⟨s, hs⟩ := R.generator_range g hg\n  obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := R.enumerate_surjective s\n  exact ⟨k + 1, hs.trans (hk ▸ R.neighborhood_subset_region k)⟩\n\n/-! #### The induced consistent stabilizer system -/\n\n/-- The consistent stabilizer system generated by the finite-range generators. -/\nnoncomputable def stabilizerSystem : FullPauliStabilizerSystem Site where\n  group := Subgroup.closure R.generators\n  involutive := fun g hg => R.toStabilizerGeneratorData.closure_involutive g hg\n  consistent := R.no_negative_identity\n\n@[simp] theorem stabilizerSystem_group :\n    R.stabilizerSystem.group = Subgroup.closure R.generators := rfl\n\n/-- Each generator is a global stabilizer. -/\ntheorem generator_mem_group {g : FullPauliWord Site} (hg : g ∈ R.generators) :\n    g ∈ R.stabilizerSystem.group :=\n  Subgroup.subset_closure hg\n\n/-- The global stabilizer group is abelian, as the generators commute. -/\ntheorem stabilizerSystem_commute (g h : R.stabilizerSystem.group) :\n    Commute (g : FullPauliWord Site) (h : FullPauliWord Site) :=\n  R.toStabilizerGeneratorData.closure_commute _ _ g.2 h.2\n\n/-! #### The increasing sequence of finite local stabilizer groups -/\n\n/--\nThe local stabilizer group `G_{S,Γ_n}` of the manuscript, seen as a subgroup of\nthe global stabilizer group: the stabilizers supported in `region n`.\n-/\nnoncomputable def localStabilizer (n : ℕ) : Subgroup ↥R.stabilizerSystem.group :=\n  ((R.stabilizerSystem.regionStabilizer (R.region n)).group).comap\n    R.stabilizerSystem.group.subtype\n\ntheorem mem_localStabilizer_iff (n : ℕ) (g : ↥R.stabilizerSystem.group) :\n    g ∈ R.localStabilizer n ↔ (g : FullPauliWord Site).label.support ⊆ R.region n := by\n  constructor\n  · intro hg\n    exact ((R.stabilizerSystem.mem_regionStabilizer_group_iff _ _).mp hg).2\n  · intro hg\n    exact (R.stabilizerSystem.mem_regionStabilizer_group_iff _ _).mpr ⟨g.2, hg⟩\n\n/-- The local stabilizer groups increase along the exhaustion. -/\ntheorem localStabilizer_mono (n m : ℕ) (hnm : n ≤ m) :\n    R.localStabilizer n ≤ R.localStabilizer m := by\n  intro g hg\n  rw [mem_localStabilizer_iff] at hg ⊢\n  exact hg.trans (R.region_mono hnm)\n\n/-- Every global stabilizer is local at some finite stage: the sequence of\nlocal stabilizer groups exhausts the stabilizer group. -/\ntheorem exists_mem_localStabilizer (g : ↥R.stabilizerSystem.group) :\n    ∃ n, g ∈ R.localStabilizer n := by\n  obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ := R.exists_region_superset (g : FullPauliWord Site).label.support\n  exact ⟨n, (R.mem_localStabilizer_iff n g).mpr hn⟩\n\n/-- The local stabilizer groups have the whole stabilizer group as supremum. -/\ntheorem iSup_localStabilizer : (⨆ n : ℕ, R.localStabilizer n) = ⊤ := by\n  refine eq_top_iff.mpr fun g _ => ?_\n  obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ := R.exists_mem_localStabilizer g\n  exact Subgroup.mem_iSup_of_mem n hn\n\n/-- Every generator is a member of some finite local stabilizer group. -/\ntheorem generator_mem_localStabilizer {g : FullPauliWord Site} (hg : g ∈ R.generators) :\n    ∃ n, (⟨g, R.generator_mem_group hg⟩ : ↥R.stabilizerSystem.group) ∈\n      R.localStabilizer n := by\n  obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ := R.generator_supportedIn_region hg\n  exact ⟨n, (R.mem_localStabilizer_iff n _).mpr hn⟩\n\n/-- **Each local stabilizer group is finite**, by finite support alone. -/\nnoncomputable instance localStabilizerFintype (n : ℕ) :\n    Fintype ↥(R.localStabilizer n) := by\n  classical\n  letI : Fintype ↥(FullPauliWord.localGroup (Site := Site) (R.region n)) :=\n    FullPauliWord.localGroupFintype _\n  have hinj : Function.Injective\n      (fun g : ↥(R.localStabilizer n) =>\n        (⟨(g : ↥R.stabilizerSystem.group), (R.mem_localStabilizer_iff n _).mp g.2⟩ :\n          ↥(FullPauliWord.localGroup (Site := Site) (R.region n)))) := by\n    intro g h hgh\n    apply Subtype.ext\n    apply Subtype.ext\n    exact congrArg (fun x : ↥(FullPauliWord.localGroup (Site := Site) (R.region n)) =>\n      (x : FullPauliWord Site)) hgh\n  have : Finite ↥(R.localStabilizer n) := Finite.of_injective _ hinj\n  exact Fintype.ofFinite _\n\n/-! #### The isolated local-code consistency condition -/\n\n# Summary of changes for run 5b3348cb-4bec-468f-b382-a5383848de2a\n## FF22 — trace and fullness of the finite-range stabilizer corner: complete\n\n**New module (the only new source file):** `FiniteFiber/FiniteRangeTracialCorner.lean` (1278 lines), plus its `import` line in `FiniteFiber.lean` and new `#print axioms` lines in `tests/AxiomAudit.lean`.\n\n**Exact build result**\n```\nlake build FiniteFiber.FiniteRangeTracialCorner   → ✔ Built FiniteFiber.FiniteRangeTracialCorner\nlake build                                        → Build completed successfully (3211 jobs).\nlake env lean tests/AxiomAudit.lean               → propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound only\n```\n(The only diagnostic is the pre-existing `manifest out of date` warning about the mathlib dependency source kind.) No `sorry`, `admit`, `axiom`, `opaque`, `unsafe` or `implemented_by` occurs in the module.\n\n### Derived vs still conditional\n\n| FF20 premise / claim | Status | Lean name | Extra hypotheses |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 2. `q ≠ 0` | derived | `FiniteRangeStabilizerSystem.cornerProjection_ne_zero'` | FF21 data `R, Q, W, M, hM` only |\n| 3. fullness (central support `1`) | derived | `FiniteRangeStabilizerSystem.cornerProjection_isFullProjection` | FF21 data only |\n| dense product orbit (local cyclicity of `Ω`) | derived | `QuasilocalStabilizerState.dense_localOperatorAlgebra_orbit` | `Q, W` only |\n| normality of `τ_q`, stated as exact strong-limit continuity | derived | `vectorFunctional_tendsto_of_strong`, `tendsto_vectorFunctional_sandwich` | none |\n| positivity `τ_q(a*a)=‖aΩ‖²`, normalization `τ_q(q)=1` | derived | `vectorFunctional_star_mul_self`, `vectorFunctional_eq_one_of_fixes` | none |\n| finite-volume trace cyclicity (Lemma `lem:finite-trace`) | derived | `FullPauliStabilizerSystem.localState_regionCodeProjector_comm` | none |\n| `p_n = π_ω(P_{Γ_n})` (identifies FF21 supports with code projectors) | derived | `FiniteRangeStabilizerSystem.supportProjection_eq_representation` | none |\n| local (finite-stage) corner traciality | derived | `FiniteRangeStabilizerSystem.cornerPairing_comm_of_mem_localOperatorAlgebra` | FF21 data |\n| 1. traciality on `q M q`, **general `M`** | conditional | `FiniteRangeStabilizerSystem.tracial_cornerProjection` | `hgen : W.GeneratedByLocalAlgebra M` (`M ⊆ π_ω(𝒜_loc)''`) |\n| 1. faithfulness on `q M q`, **general `M`** | conditional | `FiniteRangeStabilizerSystem.faithful_cornerProjection` | same `hgen` |\n| 1. traciality + faithfulness for `M = M_Γ = π_ω(𝒜_loc)''` | **derived** | `tracial_/faithful_cornerProjection_localVonNeumannAlgebra` | none beyond `R, Q, W` |\n| full `SupportCornerConclusion` for `M_Γ` | **derived** | `FiniteRangeStabilizerSystem.supportCornerConclusion_localVonNeumannAlgebra` | none beyond `R, Q, W` |\n| no-type-III conclusion | not asserted | — | deferred to FF23, as instructed |\n\n`GeneratedByLocalAlgebra M` is the packet's only extra premise, stated as an explicit Lean definition and passed as an explicit argument. It is the definitional identification `M = M_Γ` (with FF21's `hM` it reads `π_ω(𝒜_loc) ⊆ M ⊆ π_ω(𝒜_loc)''`), and it is counterexample-sensitive: for `M = B(H)`, which still satisfies `hM`, the approximation argument only yields symmetry of the corner pairing inside the strong closure of the local algebra, so the corner vector state need not be tracial. Crucially it is **discharged** for the canonical algebra, so the headline theorem carries no extra hypothesis at all.\n\n### Infrastructure built here (absent from Mathlib)\n* `exists_mem_norm_sub_apply_lt` — the von Neumann density theorem in finite-tuple strong-approximation form, proved from scratch by the amplification argument; this replaces the manuscript's appeal to Kaplansky density.\n* `bicommutant` — the bicommutant `𝒜''` of an arbitrary star subalgebra of `B(H)` packaged as a Mathlib `VonNeumannAlgebra`, and `QuasilocalStabilizerState.localVonNeumannAlgebra = π_ω(𝒜_loc)''` realizing the manuscript's `M_Γ`.\n* `cornerPairing` with `cornerPairing_comm_of_local` / `cornerPairing_comm_of_localAlgebra` — the two-vector approximation step carrying local symmetry of `Φ(x,y)=τ_q(qxqyq)` to the whole bicommutant.\n* the exact strong-limit lemmas `tendsto_apply_of_stronglyTendsTo`, `tendsto_sandwich_apply`, `cornerPairing_comm_of_eventually`, and faithfulness for arbitrary corner elements.\n\nAll work is committed and pushed; the full derived-vs-conditional table and the verification commands are also recorded in `HANDOFF.md`.\n--- FiniteFiber.lean\t2026-08-07 00:26:08.670362154 +0200\n+++ ../work/2026-08-finite-fiber-von-neumann-formalization/investigations/I004-countable-pauli-quasilocal-realization/aristotle_responses/FF22-extracted/aristotle-finite_fiber-jwxyqzjl_aristotle/FiniteFiber.lean\t2026-08-07 02:10:07.000000000 +0200\n@@ -32,3 +32,4 @@\n import FiniteFiber.CountablePauliRepresentation\n import FiniteFiber.ActualStabilizerSupportCorner\n import FiniteFiber.FiniteRangeSupportCornerConstruction\n+import FiniteFiber.FiniteRangeTracialCorner\n--- HANDOFF.md\t2026-08-06 20:11:22.801206353 +0200\n+++ ../work/2026-08-finite-fiber-von-neumann-formalization/investigations/I004-countable-pauli-quasilocal-realization/aristotle_responses/FF22-extracted/aristotle-finite_fiber-jwxyqzjl_aristotle/HANDOFF.md\t2026-08-07 02:10:07.000000000 +0200\n@@ -417,3 +417,71 @@\n Both audits report only `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`.  The\n closeout review is at\n `../work/2026-08-finite-fiber-von-neumann-formalization/investigations/I004-countable-pauli-quasilocal-realization/aristotle_responses/FF15-live-closeout-adversarial-review.md`.\n+\n+## FF22 — trace and fullness of the finite-range stabilizer corner\n+\n+New module (the only new source file): `FiniteFiber/FiniteRangeTracialCorner.lean`\n+(plus its import line in `FiniteFiber.lean` and new `#print axioms` lines in\n+`tests/AxiomAudit.lean`).\n+\n+Verification:\n+\n+```bash\n+lake build FiniteFiber.FiniteRangeTracialCorner   # ✔ Built\n+lake build                                        # Build completed succes