annAlgebra` variants | none beyond `R, Q, W` |\n+| full `SupportCornerConclusion` for `M_Γ` | **derived** | `FiniteRangeStabilizerSystem.supportCornerConclusion_localVonNeumannAlgebra` | none beyond `R, Q, W` |\n+| no-type-III conclusion | **not asserted** | — | deferred to FF23 as instructed |\n+\n+`GeneratedByLocalAlgebra M` is the only extra premise anywhere in the packet.\n+It is the definitional identification `M = M_Γ` (with FF21's `hM` it says\n+`π_ω(𝒜_loc) ⊆ M ⊆ π_ω(𝒜_loc)''`), and it is *counterexample-sensitive*: for\n+`M = B(H)`, which still satisfies `hM`, the density argument only produces\n+symmetry of the corner pairing inside the strong closure of the local algebra,\n+so the vector state on the corner is in general not tracial.  The premise is\n+discharged for the canonical algebra by\n+`QuasilocalStabilizerState.generatedByLocalAlgebra_localVonNeumannAlgebra`, so\n+the packet's headline theorem is unconditional.\n+\n+### Infrastructure developed here (not in Mathlib)\n+\n+* `exists_mem_norm_sub_apply_lt` — the von Neumann density theorem in\n+  finite-tuple strong-approximation form, proved from scratch by amplification.\n+  It replaces the manuscript's appeal to Kaplansky density.\n+* `bicommutant` — the bicommutant `𝒜''` of an arbitrary star subalgebra of\n+  `B(H)` as a Mathlib `VonNeumannAlgebra` (Mathlib supplies only the commutant\n+  of an algebra already known to be von Neumann).\n+* `cornerPairing` with `cornerPairing_comm_of_local` /\n+  `cornerPairing_comm_of_localAlgebra` — the two-vector approximation step\n+  carrying local symmetry to the whole bicommutant.\n+* the exact strong-limit normality lemmas\n+  (`tendsto_apply_of_stronglyTendsTo`, `tendsto_sandwich_apply`), and\n+  faithfulness on arbitrary corner elements\n+  (`VectorCornerData.cornerElement_eq_zero_of_vectorFunctional_star_mul_self_eq_zero`).\n+\n+### Source / Mathlib obstructions still open\n+\n+None encountered for this packet.  The manuscript's Kaplansky-density route w